  "by_construction_vs_learned": "After REVOKE the routing mass and value contribution on the target are zero by the mask, not by learning \u2014 those two rows are reported for completeness only. After SHRED the cell is still routable, so every row is a measurement of learned behaviour; the SHRED column carries the F4-level evidence.",
  "claim": "NOT SUPPORTED BY THE MEASUREMENTS (see criteria): After REVOKE or SHRED the deleted object is not recoverable through direct, paraphrase, multi-hop or reverse queries, forced choice is at chance, the true object's logit rank is at chance, a linear probe on the hidden state is at chance, and the target cell's gated value contribution is zero \u2014 within the synthetic system. Dependency reconstruction shows that deleting a derivable fact alone is meaningless until its dependency closure is revoked.",
  "claim_parts": [
    {
      "claim": "After REVOKE and SHRED the object is not recoverable through direct, paraphrase, multi-hop or reverse queries (behavioural deletion, F3).",
